-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock / Demonology: pure-DBC changes (no C++, no custom spells)
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- First file of the Demonology batch.  Everything here is a plain
-- `alonecraft_spell_dbc` override and is fully independent of the rest of the
-- batch, so it can be landed and tested on its own with:
--
--     build_and_run.bat --skip-build
--
-- Covers TODO.md items:
--   * Master Summoner              (talent, cast time + mana cost)
--   * Demonic Resilience           (talent, crit-avoid -> miss chance)
--   * Voidwalker Torment           (spell, now a real taunt)
--   * Succubus Seduction           (spell, now behaves like Fear)
--
--
-- TORMENT -> A REAL TAUNT  (ranks 3716 7809 7810 7811 11774 11775 27270 47984)
--
--   Rank chain taken from `spell_ranks`, NOT from a name search.  The IDs that
--   look like extra ranks (20317, 27490, 33703, 47965, 48000, 48005, 48006 ...)
--   are the "Teaches Voidwalker Torment (Rank N)" learn spells -- editing those
--   would break pet spell learning.  Only the 8 IDs above are real.
--
--   Torment used a single SPELL_EFFECT_THREAT (63), which merely adds a flat
--   threat lump.  Worse, Spell::EffectThreat passes ignoreModifiers = true
--   (SpellEffects.cpp:3709), so threat modifiers never touch it.
--
--   It is now modelled on warrior Taunt (355), which is:
--       Effect1 = SPELL_EFFECT_ATTACK_ME (114),  implicit target 6
--       Effect2 = APPLY_AURA / SPELL_AURA_MOD_TAUNT (11), implicit target 6
--       DurationIndex 27 (= 3000 ms, verified against SpellDuration.dbc)
--   Spell::EffectTaunt (SpellEffects.cpp:3330) then calls
--   ThreatManager::MatchUnitThreatToHighestThreat, i.e. a genuine target swap.
--
--   The original flat threat is NOT lost -- it moves to the free Effect3 slot
--   with its per-rank value intact (44/74/124/214/299/394/631/1174), so Torment
--   still builds threat between taunts.
--
--   CategoryRecoveryTime stays at 5000: a taunt on a 5s cooldown is the point.
--   The shipped tooltip already reads "Taunts the creature, increasing the
--   chance that it will attack the Voidwalker" -- now literally true, so the
--   description is left untouched.
--
--   Voidwalker Suffering already uses SPELL_EFFECT_ATTACK_ME, so ATTACK_ME is
--   proven to work on this exact pet.
--
--
-- SEDUCTION BEHAVES LIKE FEAR  (6358, single rank)
--
--   Seduction does NOT have SPELL_ATTR1_ONLY_PEACEFUL_TARGETS -- its
--   AttributesEx is 16388 (IS_CHANNELED | TRACK_TARGET_IN_CHANNEL).  Three
--   separate things made it useless in combat:
--
--   1. AuraInterruptFlags 2 -> 4718592
--      2 = AURA_INTERRUPT_FLAG_TAKE_DAMAGE: the aura dies to *any* damage,
--      including a single DoT tick (Unit.cpp:1060).  4718592 = 0x480000 is
--      what Fear (5782) carries: CHANGE_MAP | TELEPORTED, i.e. no damage break.
--
--   2. ProcFlags 0 -> 664232, ProcChance 101 -> 100  (both copied from Fear)
--      A breakable-CC aura with non-zero ProcFlags gets a damage pool from
--      AuraEffect::CalculateAmount (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:493), sized
--      CreatureBaseStats(casterLevel, WARRIOR)->BaseHealth[EXPANSION_WOTLK]/4.75.
--      CheckEffectProc (:1206) and HandleBreakableCCAuraProc (:1294) drain it,
--      so damage now *accumulates* toward a break instead of breaking instantly.
--      SPELL_AURA_MOD_STUN is already in the handled CC list, so the aura type
--      does not change.
--
--   3. ChannelInterruptFlags 31804 -> 19516  (clears 0x1000 | 0x2000)
--      0x1000 = MELEE_ATTACK, 0x2000 = SPELL_ATTACK.  The Succubus's own
--      auto-attack was shattering its own channel, and a broken channel ends
--      the aura.  Same fix Infernal Bargain needed in woa_2026_08_02_00.sql.
--      Everything else in the field is kept, including 0x8 (INTERRUPT) and
--      0x4 (CAST).  Verified these bits are read as AURA_INTERRUPT_FLAG_*
--      values at Unit.cpp:5490.
--
--   The caster is the Succubus, so the damage pool scales off the pet's level,
--   which for a summoned demon equals the owner's level.
--
--   Core's spell_warl_seduction (spell_warlock.cpp:161) only strips DoTs for
--   Glyph of Succubus and is unaffected by all of the above.
--
--
-- MASTER SUMMONER  (18709 / 18710)
--
--   -2s/-20% and -4s/-40% become -4s/-40% and -8s/-80%.  Base demon summons
--   are a 10s cast, so rank 2 lands at 2s.
--
--   The existing EffectSpellClassMask 0x20000000 on both effects already covers
--   all five summons (688 Imp / 697 Voidwalker / 712 Succubus / 691 Felhunter /
--   30146 Felguard) -- verified, so the masks are left alone.  There is no
--   Incubus in creature_template (only 416/417/1860/1863/17252), so the TODO's
--   mention of one is a no-op.
--
--   Descriptions are rewritten with literal numbers rather than $/1000;s1,
--   which renders the stored negative value as "-4 sec" on a line that already
--   says "reduces by".
--
--
-- DEMONIC RESILIENCE  (30319 / 30320 / 30321)
--
--   "Hit instead of critically hit": the crit-avoidance auras become
--   miss-chance auras, keeping the same magnitudes (1/2/3%).
--       Effect1  187 MOD_ATTACKER_MELEE_CRIT_CHANCE -> 184 MOD_ATTACKER_MELEE_HIT_CHANCE
--       Effect3  179 MOD_ATTACKER_SPELL_CRIT_CHANCE -> 186 MOD_ATTACKER_SPELL_HIT_CHANCE
--   BasePoints are unchanged (-2/-3/-4 with DieSides 1 -> -1/-2/-3%).
--
--   Effect2 is currently DEAD: SPELL_AURA_ADD_FLAT_MODIFIER, MiscValue 8, with
--   EffectSpellClassMaskB2 = 16384 -- a mask that matches no warlock spell.
--   Nothing in src/server/ references 30319/30320/30321 and `spell_pet_auras`
--   has no row for it, so the advertised "reduces all damage your summoned
--   demon takes" has never done anything.
--
--   It becomes SPELL_AURA_DUMMY, keeping BasePoints -6/-11/-16 (-> -5/-10/-15)
--   as the pet damage-reduction percentage, with MiscValue and the stray B2
--   mask cleared.  That dummy is the `spell_pet_auras` anchor; the row that
--   delivers custom aura 200421 to the demon lands in woa_2026_08_02_04.sql.
--   A dummy effect with no matching spell_pet_auras row is inert, so this file
--   remains safe to land on its own.
--


